{% extends "base_analyze.prompt" %}

{% block specific_task %}
<specific_task>
Generate PREDICTIONS - forecasts about future campaign performance based on current trends and data patterns.

Focus on "what will likely happen" based on observable trends. Predictions should:
- Forecast future metrics or outcomes based on current trajectory
- Project end-of-campaign results (total spend, conversions, ROAS, etc.)
- Identify likely scenarios if current trends continue
- Warn about potential issues before they occur
- Highlight opportunities that may emerge

Examples of good predictions:
- "At current pacing, campaign will end with $1,200 unspent (15% under budget)"
- "If CTR continues declining at current rate (-2% daily), it will drop below 0.5% by day 10"
- "Based on improving conversion trends, campaign will likely exceed ROAS target of 2.0x by end date"

{% include "priorities_guidelines.snippet" %}
</specific_task>

<output_format>
**CRITICAL: Your response must be ONLY valid JSON. Do not include markdown, explanations, code fences, or any text outside the JSON array.**

Return a JSON array of prediction findings with this exact structure:

[
  {
    "priority": "low" | "high",
    "sentiment": "positive" | "neutral" | "negative",
    "data": {
      "description": "Forecast of future performance or outcome (1 sentence)",
      "rationale": "Data patterns and logic supporting this prediction (1 sentence)",
      "summary": "Super concise summary of the prediction (a few words)",
      "supporting_metrics": {
        "metric_name": numeric_value
      }
    }
  }
]

Your response must start with [ and end with ]. Nothing else.
</output_format>
{% endblock %}
